# Keepalive recovery (the Relay-parented `sleep infinity` held by the task)
first version (logon trigger + RestartCount on failure only):
23:11:17 kill -TERM keepalive -> 23:14:45 not restarted; task State=Ready LastTaskResult=0 NextRunTime=(none)
  => conhost --headless exits 0 whatever wsl.exe returns (wsl.exe itself exited 15 for a killed session), so
     restart-on-failure never fires, and a logon trigger's repetition only starts at the next logon.
fixed version (added time trigger, every minute, IgnoreNew):
23:15:07 re-registered -> 23:16:07 keepalive started by the time trigger (pid start 23:16:07)
23:16:16 kill -TERM keepalive -> back after 92s; then 2 further re-fires observed: instances=1 (IgnoreNew, no duplicates)

